{'symbol': 'INCY', 'date': '2020-09-14 09:30:00', 'title': 'Baricitinib In Combination With Remdesivir Reduces Time To Recovery In Hospitalized Patients With Covid-19 In NIAID-Sponsored ACTT-2 Trial', 'text': "BARICITINIB IN COMBINATION WITH REMDESIVIR REDUCES TIME TO RECOVERY IN HOSPITALIZED PATIENTS WITH COVID-19 IN NIAID-SPONSORED ACTT-2 TRIAL.INCYTE CORP - STUDY MET PRIMARY ENDPOINT OF REDUCTION OF TIME TO RECOVERY.INCYTE CORP - ADDITIONAL ANALYSES ONGOING TO UNDERSTAND OTHER CLINICAL OUTCOME DATA.INCYTE CORP - LILLY'S PHASE 3 RANDOMIZED, DOUBLE-BLIND, PLACEBO-CONTROLLED STUDY OF BARICITINIB CONTINUES.INCYTE CORP - BARICITINIB IN COMBINATION WITH REMDESIVIR MET PRIMARY ENDPOINT OF REDUCTION OF TIME TO RECOVERY IN COMPARISON WITH REMDESIVIR..INCYTE CORP - ADDITIONAL ANALYSES ARE ONGOING TO UNDERSTAND OTHER CLINICAL OUTCOME DATA, INCLUDING MORTALITY AND SAFETY DATA.INCYTE CORP - NIAID IS EXPECTED TO PUBLISH FULL DETAILS OF STUDY IN A PEER-REVIEWED JOURNAL..INCYTE CORP -  LILLY PLANS TO DISCUSS POTENTIAL FOR EMERGENCY USE AUTHORIZATION (EUA) WITH U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION FOR BARICITINIB.INCYTE CORP - LILLY TO EXPLORE SIMILAR MEASURES WITH OTHER REGULATORY AGENCIES FOR BARICITINIB AS A TREATMENT OF HOSPITALIZED PATIENTS WITH COVID-19."}
